      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline TiVNbTa alloy has a yield strength of approximately 330 MPa at 1273 K.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial alloy is processed by solution treatment at approximately 1600 K.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 0.5–1.0 at% carbon and aging at approximately 1100 K for 1–4 hours will promote in situ carbide precipitation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitated carbide will be TiC.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The TiC precipitates will be nanoscale.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The TiC precipitates will be uniformly dispersed within the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoscale TiC precipitates will obstruct dislocation motion at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoscale TiC precipitates will inhibit grain-boundary sliding at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Obstructing dislocation motion and grain-boundary sliding will reduce creep and thermal softening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon doping and aging will increase the 1273 K yield strength from approximately 330 MPa to more than 450–500 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The strengthened alloy will reasonably maintain ductility relative to the undoped baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted improvement applies at 1273 K under compressive loading to strains of 30%.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Performance and microstructural stability outside the stated thermal and mechanical boundaries are uncertain.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitate size, distribution, and volume fraction will affect the magnitude of high-temperature strengthening.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon solubility and TiC-nucleation kinetics may cause deviations from the predicted property improvement.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
